@startuml
title Hypothesis A - Abstract Component View

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

actor "Researcher" as researcher

package "Evaluation Input" as input_area {
  artifact "Process Descriptions\nand Test Cases" as process_inputs
  artifact "Generated n8n\nWorkflow Candidates" as workflow_candidates
}

package "Local Test Environment" as test_area {
  component "Test Runner" as test_runner
  component "n8n Runtime" as n8n
  component "Simulated Business Systems" as simulated_systems
}

package "Simulated Business Systems" as systems_detail {
  component "ERP / CRM" as erp
  component "Email" as email
  component "Database" as database
  component "Document Store" as dms
  component "External APIs" as apis
}

package "Evaluation Output" as output_area {
  artifact "Execution Logs" as execution_logs
  artifact "Observed Results" as observed_results
  artifact "Hypothesis A Metrics" as metrics
}

researcher --> test_runner : starts evaluation
process_inputs --> test_runner : test inputs\nexpected outcomes
workflow_candidates --> test_runner : workflows under test

test_runner --> n8n : imports and triggers\nworkflow runs
n8n --> simulated_systems : executes process\nagainst mocked systems
simulated_systems --> n8n : controlled responses

simulated_systems .. erp
simulated_systems .. email
simulated_systems .. database
simulated_systems .. dms
simulated_systems .. apis

n8n --> execution_logs : execution traces
n8n --> observed_results : workflow outcomes
test_runner --> metrics : success rates\nruntime\nfailure classes

note right of metrics
Hypothesis A asks whether generated
workflows complete successfully under
repeated realistic test conditions.
end note

note bottom of simulated_systems
The business systems are local simulations.
They make the test reproducible while still
requiring real workflow execution.
end note

@enduml
